{"type":"message","message":{"id":"gen-1775392480-Oq84wMmGRi3rIsM0DmzO","role":"assistant","created":1775392494,"content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have the data. Let me extract the NASA outlay data for FY 2008-2017:\n\nFrom the 2012 document (page 24):\n- 2008: 17,834\n- 2009: 19,168\n- 2010: 18,906\n- 2011: 17,617\n- 2012: 17,190\n\nFrom the 2017 document (page 22):\n- 2013: 16,978\n- 2014: 17,093\n- 2015: 18,272\n- 2016: 18,828\n- 2017: 18,698\n\nThese are in millions of dollars. I need to find the \"total on-budget and off-budget outlay\". Looking at the table, the columns are:\n- National Aeronautics and Space Administration (25) - this is NASA\n- Total outlays On-budget (35)\n- Total outlays Off-budget (36)\n\nThe question asks for \"total on-budget and off-budget outlay for NASA\". This is a bit ambiguous - it could mean:\n1. Just NASA's outlay (the column for NASA), which already represents total outlays\n2. NASA on-budget + NASA off-budget\n\nLooking at the table, the NASA column (25) seems to be the total outlay for NASA (both on and off budget combined). But wait - there are separate \"On-budget\" and \"Off-budget\" columns at the end for the Total, not for each agency.\n\nActually, looking more carefully at the table structure:\n- Column 25 is NASA (the agency's total outlay)\n- Columns 35 and 36 are \"Total outlays On-budget\" and \"Total outlays Off-budget\" (for the whole government)\n\nSo the NASA column (17,834 for 2008, etc.) is already the total NASA outlay. But the question specifically says \"on-budget and off-budget outlay\" which suggests we might need to add them.\n\n\nI realize the 2012 document only provides NASA figures through 2012, while the 2017 document covers 2013-2017. Both sources consistently show a single NASA outlay figure per year, indicating this represents the complete NASA expenditure across both budget categories. The data suggests the total is already consolidated, with no separate breakdown available.\n","signature":""},{"type":"toolRequest","id":"call_fa6f7f81728b4146af597190","toolCall":{"status":"success","value":{"name":"shell","arguments":{"command":"python3 << 'EOF'\n# NASA outlay data from Treasury Bulletin documents (in millions)\n# FY 2008-2012 from 2012 Bulletin page 24\n# FY 2013-2017 from 2017 Bulletin page 22\n\nnasa_outlays = {\n    2008: 17834,\n    2009: 19168,\n    2010: 18906,\n    2011: 17617,\n    2012: 17190,\n    2013: 16978,\n    2014: 17093,\n    2015: 18272,\n    2016: 18828,\n    2017: 18698\n}\n\n# Convert to billions\nvalues = [v / 1000 for v in nasa_outlays.values()]\nprint(\"NASA outlay (in billions):\")\nfor year, val in nasa_outlays.items():\n    print(f\"  {year}: {val} million = {val/1000:.3f} billion\")\n\nprint(f\"\\nValues in billions: {values}\")\n\n# Sort values for Winsorization\nsorted_values = sorted(values)\nprint(f\"Sorted values: {sorted_values}\")\n\n# 10% Winsorized: replace bottom 10% and top 10% with next values\nn = len(values)\nlower_pct = 0.10\nupper_pct = 0.10\n\n# For 10% Winsorized, we replace values below the 10th percentile with the 10th percentile value\n# and values above the 90th percentile with the 90th percentile value\nlower_idx = int(n * lower_pct)\nupper_idx = n - 1 - int(n * upper_pct)\n\nprint(f\"n = {n}, lower_idx = {lower_idx}, upper_idx = {upper_idx}\")\nprint(f\"Lower bound value (10th pct): {sorted_values[lower_idx]}\")\nprint(f\"Upper bound value (90th pct): {sorted_values[upper_idx]}\")\n\n# Winsorized values\nwinsorized = values.copy()\nwinsorized = [max(v, sorted_values[lower_idx]) for v in winsorized]\nwinsorized = [min(v, sorted_values[upper_idx]) for v in winsorized]\n\nprint(f\"Winsorized values: {winsorized}\")\n\n# 10% Winsorized range = max - min of winsorized values\nwinsorized_min = min(winsorized)\nwinsorized_max = max(winsorized)\nwinsorized_range = winsorized_max - winsorized_min\n\nprint(f\"\\nWinsorized min: {winsorized_min:.4f}\")\nprint(f\"Winsorized max: {winsorized_max:.4f}\")\nprint(f\"10% Winsorized range: {winsorized_range:.4f}\")\nprint(f\"\\nRounded to hundredths: {winsorized_range:.2f} billion dollars\")\nEOF"}}},"_meta":{"goose_extension":"developer"}}],"metadata":{"userVisible":true,"agentVisible":true}}}
